    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-impact production today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier start with an 83.29 efficiency score. Facing Johnson, R, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite 4.96 xERA matchup and a massive park factor boost, making him a cornerstone for power and run production. **Luis Robert Jr.** (66.61) and **Drake Baldwin** (65.79) follow closely as strong starts; **Luis Robert Jr.** leverages a favorable platoon split against Griffin (L) and a slow-delivering pitcher that creates a high-upside environment for his stolen base profile. **Drake Baldwin** is riding high on a strong lead-off spot assignment, maximizing his total opportunity to anchor our daily offensive output.\n\nOur decision-making process was most tested by the fringe of the starting rotation, specifically regarding **Luis Lara** (37.66). While **Luis Lara** possesses the switch-hitting versatility we value, his matchup against Ashcraft, B\u2014a pitcher with a respectable 3.35 xERA\u2014drove his score below our strict 40.0 floor. We opted for the safer efficiency of **Wade Meckler** (59.97), whose top-of-the-order status and favorable park factors provide a higher, more reliable floor. We are continuing to monitor **Nasim Nunez** (40.23); he remains active, but he faces a stiff challenge against S\u00e1nchez, C (2.86 xERA). His involvement is strictly limited by the defensive profile of the opposing catcher and a high-efficiency hold pitcher, which effectively stifles his primary value as a base stealer. \n\nRegarding roster integrity, we remain vigilant as **Jordan Westburg** remains sidelined on the IL, and key contributors like **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** are inactive due to scheduled days off. We are also tracking the development of prospects like **Sam Antonacci** and **Liam Hicks** for potential spot-start utility, but for today, the focus is squarely on our core to capitalize on the weak pitching staff facing **Dominic Smith** and **Jackson Merrill**. Managers should note that while **Miguel Vargas** holds a marginal score of 51.78, his BvP and xwOBA profile suggest he is under-projected, provided he can navigate the difficult presence of Suarez (L) on the mound.",
